1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Hello. Welcome to Daily English Talk.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Hi, everyone. We are so happy you are here.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
I'm Emma. And I'm Jack. On this channel, we help you practice English with real conversations.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Please, if you like our video, remember to subscribe and like it. It helps us a lot.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Today, we are going to talk about a very fun topic.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,280
Yes, we are talking all about vacation.

7
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:33,840
I love vacation. Let's get started.

8
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:37,440
So, Jack, how are you today?

9
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,760
I am very good, thank you. And you?

10
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,960
I'm great. The weather is nice today. I like the sun.

11
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:49,040
Me too. Sunshine is good. So, what did you do this weekend?

12
00:00:49,040 --> 00:00:58,840
This weekend? Oh, I stayed home. I watched a movie and read a book. It was very relaxing.

13
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:03,160
That sounds nice. My weekend was gizzy. I visited my family.

14
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:06,440
Oh, that's lovely. Did you have a good time?

15
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,440
Yes, I did. My mom cooked my favorite food.

16
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:12,080
Wonderful. I'm happy for you.

17
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:16,480
Thanks, Emma. I'm happy to be here now to talk about vacations.

18
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:22,060
Okay, Jack. Let's talk about vacations. Do you like vacations?

19
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,460
Do I like vacations? Of course. Everyone likes vacations. It's the best.

20
00:01:27,460 --> 00:01:31,000
That's true. What is your favorite type of vacation?

21
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:38,020
My favorite type. Hmm. Let me think. I really, really like beach vacations.

22
00:01:38,020 --> 00:01:40,960
The beach? Why do you like it so much?

23
00:01:40,960 --> 00:01:42,740
I love the ocean.

24
00:01:42,740 --> 00:01:45,660
The sound of the waves is so relaxing.

25
00:01:45,660 --> 00:01:47,620
I like to swim in the sea.

26
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:50,380
I like to sit on the sand and read a book.

27
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:52,340
It is very peaceful.

28
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:54,860
Oh, that does sound peaceful.

29
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:56,900
I like the beach too,

30
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:00,100
but my favorite vacation is in the mountains.

31
00:02:00,100 --> 00:02:01,380
The mountains?

32
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,460
What do you do there?

33
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:04,380
It sounds quiet.

34
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:07,300
It is quiet and that's why I like it.

35
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:09,340
I like to go for long walks.

36
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:11,440
We call that hiking.

37
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:15,320
I look at the tall trees and the clean rivers.

38
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:17,680
The air is so fresh and cool.

39
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,960
Hiking is good exercise,

40
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:23,320
but I prefer to relax on my vacation.

41
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:25,440
I don't want to walk too much.

42
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,720
Hiking is relaxing for me.

43
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:29,140
It's not a race.

44
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:32,240
I walk slowly and enjoy the nature.

45
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:34,480
Okay, I understand.

46
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:37,240
So where was your last vacation?

47
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,240
Tell me about it.

48
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:41,400
My last vacation was in Canada.

49
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,760
I visited my cousin who lives in Toronto.

50
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,600
Canada?

51
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,560
Wow, that is a big country.

52
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,640
Was it cold?

53
00:02:47,640 --> 00:02:52,480
Yes, it was a little cold even in summer, but it was okay.

54
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:55,160
We visited many, many lakes.

55
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:58,600
The lakes in Canada are huge and blue.

56
00:02:58,600 --> 00:02:59,900
That sounds nice.

57
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,640
Did you like the food in Canada?

58
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:03,680
The food was very good.

59
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:06,380
My cousin cooked for me every day.

60
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:08,660
I tried something called poutine.

61
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:09,540
Poutine?

62
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,380
What is that?

63
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:11,460
I never heard that word.

64
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:14,780
It is french fries with cheese curds

65
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:17,700
and a special brown sauce.

66
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:21,340
It was very tasty, but a little messy to eat.

67
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:26,340
Hmm, that sounds interesting and maybe a little strange.

68
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:28,260
I wanna try it one day.

69
00:03:28,260 --> 00:03:33,260
So, do you prefer summer vacations or winter vacations?

70
00:03:33,460 --> 00:03:35,540
That's a good question.

71
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,500
I think I prefer summer vacations.

72
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:41,420
I like warm weather and long sunny days.

73
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:42,420
Me too.

74
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:44,740
I don't like being cold.

75
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:50,060
For a winter vacation, I want to go to a warm place, like a tropical island.

76
00:03:50,060 --> 00:03:51,180
Smart idea.

77
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:54,620
So what do you always take with you on vacation?

78
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:55,780
What is in your bag?

79
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:58,820
Oh, I always take my swimsuit.

80
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:01,820
Even if I go to the mountains in winter, I take it.

81
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,140
Maybe there's a hot pool.

82
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:05,420
You really love swimming.

83
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:07,380
I always take my camera.

84
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:11,020
I love taking photos of everything.

85
00:04:11,020 --> 00:04:14,220
The food, the buildings, the people.

86
00:04:14,220 --> 00:04:15,700
That's a good one.

87
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:17,460
I take my phone for photos,

88
00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:20,400
but a camera is better for good pictures.

89
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,220
Yes, it is.

90
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,900
Do you like to plan your vacation a lot

91
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:27,540
or do you like to be spontaneous?

92
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:29,220
Spun...

93
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:30,500
Spun-taneous?

94
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,420
What does that mean?

95
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:32,620
It's a new word for me.

96
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:35,300
It means you don't plan everything.

97
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:38,980
You decide things at the last minute, you see what happens.

98
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:46,740
Oh, I understand. Thank you. No, I am not very spontaneous. I like to plan.

99
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:50,100
I book the hotel and the flight many months early.

100
00:04:50,100 --> 00:04:56,820
I am the same. I like to have a plan. It makes me feel calm and safe. I don't like surprises.

101
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:59,860
Exactly. If I don't have a hotel booking, I feel

102
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:07,000
I love the culture. It is so different. I want to see Tokyo, the big city. I want to see the cherry blossoms in spring and I really, really want to try the food.

103
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,960
sushi, ramen, tempura.

104
00:05:31,960 --> 00:05:32,960
Yes!

105
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:35,980
I am very excited to go one day.

106
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:37,960
What is your dream vacation, Jack?

107
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,800
My dream vacation is in Brazil.

108
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:43,900
I want to see the carnival in Rio de Janeiro.

109
00:05:43,900 --> 00:05:47,840
It looks so fun and colorful with music and dancing everywhere.

110
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:50,640
Oh, that would be a big adventure!

111
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:54,200
Do you like long vacations or short vacations?

112
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:56,660
I like long vacations.

113
00:05:56,660 --> 00:06:02,220
week or two weeks, you have more time to relax and you don't think about work.

114
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:09,640
I agree. A short vacation of two or three days is too fast. You come home and you feel tired,

115
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:10,640
not relaxed.

116
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:18,220
Yes, exactly. How do you travel to your vacations? By plane? By train? By car?

117
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:25,020
I usually travel by plane. It is fast for long distances. But I like trains too. You

118
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:27,780
You can see the countryside from the window.

119
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:28,780
It's beautiful.

120
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:30,500
I get a little nervous on planes.

121
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:35,500
The takeoff is scary for me, but for long distances, it is the best way.

122
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:36,880
I understand.

123
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:40,620
Do you stay in hotels or in apartments?

124
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:42,680
I usually stay in hotels.

125
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,860
I like hotel breakfasts.

126
00:06:44,860 --> 00:06:49,940
You can eat so much food, eggs, bread, fruit, coffee.

127
00:06:49,940 --> 00:06:51,960
Hotel breakfasts are the best.

128
00:06:51,960 --> 00:06:53,040
So much choice.

129
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,260
I love it.

130
00:06:54,260 --> 00:07:01,700
I know. Sometimes I stay in an apartment. It is cheaper and you can cook your own food, like at home.

131
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:04,660
That's true. Cooking on vacation can save money.

132
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,580
Do you buy souvenirs?

133
00:07:06,580 --> 00:07:11,380
Souvenirs. You mean gifts for friends and family?

134
00:07:11,380 --> 00:07:16,100
Yes, and for yourself. A small thing to remember the trip.

135
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:23,860
I always buy a magnet from my fridge. It is a small, cheap souvenir. My fridge is full of

136
00:07:23,860 --> 00:07:27,940
magnets from all my trips. It's like a map of my travels.

137
00:07:28,180 --> 00:07:32,660
That's a great idea. I buy postcards. I don't send them.

138
00:07:32,700 --> 00:07:36,780
I just keep them in a book. I write on the back what I did that day.

139
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:42,300
That's very nice. So what is the most beautiful place you visited?

140
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:47,540
The most beautiful place. I think it was Norway.

141
00:07:47,860 --> 00:07:50,540
The fjords are incredible.

142
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:53,880
The water is between big, big mountains,

143
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:56,080
so quiet and beautiful.

144
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:59,340
I saw photos, it looks amazing.

145
00:07:59,340 --> 00:08:04,340
For me, the most beautiful place was Greece, I think.

146
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:08,520
The White Houses and the Blue Sea is like a picture.

147
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:10,940
Do you think vacations are important?

148
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:13,480
Yes, I do, they are very important.

149
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:17,780
We work hard, we need a break, we need to rest our minds.

150
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:24,660
I agree. It is good for your mental health. You come back home feeling new and happy?

151
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:32,020
Feeling new. I like that. It's true. Do you ever have a bad vacation? A vacation with problems?

152
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:39,860
A bad vacation? Oh yes. One time, my flight was cancelled. I had to wait at the airport

153
00:08:39,860 --> 00:08:48,340
for twelve hours. It was so boring. Oh no, that is a nightmare. I am sorry. Airports

154
00:08:48,340 --> 00:08:54,820
are not fun for twelve hours. It was not fun, but in the end, I got on another flight,

155
00:08:54,820 --> 00:09:01,780
so it was okay. Did you have a bad vacation? Oh, one time I lost my bag at the airport.

156
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:06,420
It had all my clothes inside, my shirts, my pants, everything.

157
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:10,980
Oh, Jack! That is terrible! What did you do?

158
00:09:10,980 --> 00:09:18,260
I had to buy new clothes. It was very expensive. I was sad, but I got my bag back after three days.

159
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:21,860
I'm glad you got it back. That is a big vacation problem.

160
00:09:21,860 --> 00:09:30,420
Yes, a very big problem. So, let's talk about good things. What is your favorite vacation memory?

161
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:38,820
My favorite memory. I was in Italy in a small city called Venice. I was eating gelato,

162
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:46,100
looking at an old church. The sun was setting. The sky was orange and pink. It was perfect.

163
00:09:46,100 --> 00:09:51,540
That sounds like a movie. Beautiful. My favorite memory was from Greece,

164
00:09:52,260 --> 00:09:58,420
swimming in the sea at night. The water was warm and you could see thousands of stars in the sky.

165
00:09:58,420 --> 00:09:59,920
WONDERFUL

166
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,880
Hello. Do you like to try new food on vacation?

167
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:09,360
Of course. Trying new food is one of the best parts of traveling. I always look for local restaurants.

168
00:10:09,360 --> 00:10:14,000
Me too. Even if I don't know the name of the food, I just point and say,

169
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,720
I'll have that please. It's a surprise.

170
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:23,600
It's an adventure for your mouth. Sometimes it's good, sometimes it's… interesting.

171
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:28,640
That's a funny way to say it. But it's true. Do you learn a few words in the local language?

172
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:35,080
Oh, I try. I always learn hello, thank you, and goodbye. It is polite, and people smile

173
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:36,080
when you try.

174
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:41,920
Yes, it is. People are happy when you try to speak their language, even just a little.

175
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:47,680
For sure. So, Emma, what is your plan for your next vacation? Do you know yet?

176
00:10:47,680 --> 00:10:56,040
My next vacation? I am planning to go to Spain. I want to see Barcelona and Madrid. I hear

177
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:58,160
the art is amazing.

178
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:04,240
Spain is fantastic. The architecture is beautiful and the people are friendly.

179
00:11:04,240 --> 00:11:09,920
Yes, I am very excited to go one day. What is your dream vacation, Jack?

180
00:11:09,920 --> 00:11:16,560
My dream vacation is in Brazil. I want to see the carnival in Rio de Janeiro. It looks

181
00:11:16,560 --> 00:11:20,440
so fun and colorful with music and dancing everywhere.

182
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:26,760
Oh, that would be a big adventure. Do you like long vacations or short vacations?

183
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:29,360
I like long vacations.

184
00:11:29,360 --> 00:11:35,160
One week or two weeks, you have more time to relax and you don't think about work.

185
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:36,240
I agree.

186
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:39,900
A short vacation of two or three days is too fast.

187
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:43,080
You come home and you feel tired, not relaxed.

188
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:45,160
Yes, exactly.

189
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:47,460
How do you travel to your vacations?

190
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:48,560
By plane?

191
00:11:48,560 --> 00:11:49,680
By train?

192
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:50,680
By car?

193
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:53,500
I usually travel by plane.

194
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:55,960
It is fast for long distances.

195
00:11:55,960 --> 00:12:00,880
I like trains too. You can see the countryside from the window. It's beautiful.

196
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:05,440
I get a little nervous on planes. The takeoff is scary for me, but for long

197
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,640
distances, it is the best way.

198
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:12,160
I understand. Do you stay in hotels or in apartments?

199
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:17,160
Oh, I have a list on my phone for packing. It helps me remember everything.

200
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:21,600
A list? That is very, very good idea. I should do that.

201
00:12:21,600 --> 00:12:23,760
My brain is not good for remembering.

202
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:29,600
You should. It makes packing so much easier. Do you like to listen to music when you travel?

203
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:39,360
Yes. On the plane or on the train, I listen to music. It makes the time pass faster. I have a special travel playlist.

204
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:45,440
Same for me. I also like to look out the window and just watch the world go by.

205
00:12:45,440 --> 00:12:48,440
That is nice too, especially on a train.

206
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:54,440
So, we both love vacations, but what do you miss about home when you travel?

207
00:12:54,440 --> 00:12:57,440
I miss my own bed.

208
00:12:57,440 --> 00:13:01,440
Hotel beds are nice, but my bed is the best.

209
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:04,440
And I miss my morning coffee from my own kitchen.

210
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:07,440
I understand. I miss my pets. I have a cat.

211
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:11,440
I always ask my friend to send me photos of her when I'm away.

212
00:13:11,440 --> 00:13:17,000
Aww, that's sweet. Do you prefer traveling with a group or alone?

213
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:22,540
Hmm, I like traveling with one or two good friends. Alone is okay, but it's more fun

214
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:25,680
to share the experience. What about you?

215
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:31,000
I think the same. With friends, you can talk about the things you see. Alone can be a little

216
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,680
lonely sometimes.

217
00:13:32,680 --> 00:14:07,410
Yes. Emma, that was a really fun talk about vacations.

218
00:14:07,410 --> 00:14:10,130
We used a lot of good English words.

219
00:14:10,130 --> 00:14:11,690
We did.

220
00:14:11,690 --> 00:14:16,330
Maybe we can talk about some of those words again for our viewers, you know, to help them

221
00:14:16,330 --> 00:14:17,330
remember.

222
00:14:17,330 --> 00:14:18,530
That's a wonderful idea.

223
00:14:18,530 --> 00:14:21,170
Let's do a mini vocabulary review.

224
00:14:21,170 --> 00:14:23,570
We can explain the words simply.

225
00:14:23,570 --> 00:14:24,570
Perfect.

226
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:28,170
Okay, let's start with a word you said, Jack.

227
00:14:28,170 --> 00:14:29,170
Souvenir.

228
00:14:29,170 --> 00:14:30,570
Ah, yes, souvenir.

229
00:14:30,570 --> 00:14:34,210
I said I buy a magnet as a souvenir.

230
00:14:34,210 --> 00:14:39,630
So a souvenir is something you buy to help you remember a place you visited.

231
00:14:39,630 --> 00:14:41,550
Can you give another example of a souvenir?

232
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:42,550
Of course.

233
00:14:42,550 --> 00:14:44,750
A souvenir can be many things.

234
00:14:44,750 --> 00:14:51,390
A keychain with the name of a city, a postcard, a t-shirt, or a small statue.

235
00:14:51,390 --> 00:14:55,110
It's a memory from your trip that you can hold in your hands.

236
00:14:55,110 --> 00:14:58,070
And it's not usually very expensive, right?

237
00:14:58,070 --> 00:14:59,950
It's a small gift for yourself.

238
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Yes, exactly. My sister always asks me, Jack, did you bring me a souvenir? So I have to buy one for her too.

239
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:12,000
That's nice. Okay, the next word is one I used. Hiking.

240
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Yes, you said you love hiking in the mountains. So what does it mean exactly?

241
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Hiking means walking in nature for fun or exercise. It's not a walk in the city to the shops, it's a walk on a path in the mountains,

242
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:31,240
mountains, in a forest, or by a river.

243
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:35,200
So if I go for a walk in the park in my town, is that hiking?

244
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,200
Good question.

245
00:15:36,200 --> 00:15:41,800
A short walk in the town park is usually just called a walk.

246
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:47,200
Hiking is usually longer and in a more natural place, like a national park.

247
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,280
I see.

248
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:50,440
And you need good shoes for hiking, right?

249
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,680
Oh yes, very important.

250
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:55,440
You need strong, comfortable shoes.

251
00:15:55,440 --> 00:15:57,080
We call them hiking boots.

252
00:15:57,080 --> 00:16:02,840
don't want to wear sandals for hiking. No, that would be a bad idea. Okay, I understand

253
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:08,600
hiking now. It's a walk in nature. Correct. The next word is a little more difficult,

254
00:16:08,600 --> 00:16:15,320
spontaneous. Spontaneous? That was a new word for me today. Can you explain it again, Emma?

255
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:24,040
Of course. Spontaneous means you do something without a lot of planning. You decide to do it

256
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:26,760
suddenly, at the moment, it's not planned.

257
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:30,360
So, can you give me an example of a spontaneous vacation?

258
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:36,840
Yes. For example, if on Friday after work, your friend calls and says,

259
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:42,520
let's go to the beach this weekend. And you say, yes, and you go. That is a spontaneous trip.

260
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:48,200
And that is not me. I am the opposite of spontaneous. I am a planner.

261
00:16:48,200 --> 00:16:56,360
Yes, you are. The opposite of spontaneous is planned or organized. So a spontaneous person

262
00:16:56,360 --> 00:17:01,400
is often surprised and a planned person is rarely surprised.

263
00:17:01,400 --> 00:17:06,120
I like to be prepared. But maybe being spontaneous is fun sometimes.

264
00:17:06,120 --> 00:17:12,440
Maybe we can try it one day. Now another word we both used, dream vacation.

265
00:17:12,440 --> 00:17:19,800
Ah, my favorite topic. A dream vacation is the vacation you want most in the world.

266
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:24,440
It's your number one choice. It's the vacation you dream about.

267
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:31,160
Yes, it's often a special or expensive vacation, maybe a place that is far away.

268
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:34,680
It's not a normal vacation, it's a special one.

269
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:39,880
For example, my dream vacation is Brazil. It's not a simple weekend trip,

270
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:43,080
It's a big, exciting plan for the future.

271
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:51,800
Exactly. So viewers, what is your dream vacation? Think about it. Now, let's talk about another word,

272
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:58,280
local. Local. I think I said local food or local restaurants.

273
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:06,600
You did. Local means from this place, from this area. So local food is the food that people

274
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:10,360
in that place eat every day. It's traditional food for them.

275
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:18,120
So in Italy, pizza is local food. In Japan, sushi is local food. It's not food from another country.

276
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:24,120
Right. And a local person is someone who lives in that place. If you are lost,

277
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:27,000
you can ask a local person for directions.

278
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:32,600
That's a very good tip. Always ask a local person for help. They know the best places.

279
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:36,200
Definitely. Okay, one more word. Relaxing.

280
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,040
We use this word many times.

281
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:41,680
Relaxing is a very important word for vacation.

282
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:42,520
It is.

283
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,120
What does it mean, Jack?

284
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:49,120
Relaxing means calm, peaceful, not busy or stressful.

285
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:52,560
It makes you feel happy and quiet.

286
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:56,360
When I sit on the beach and read, I feel relaxed.

287
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:58,720
That activity is relaxing.

288
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,640
Perfect explanation.

289
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:03,720
So for me, hiking is relaxing.

290
00:19:03,720 --> 00:19:06,920
For you, swimming is relaxing.

291
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:10,120
Different activities can be relaxing for different people.

292
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:15,120
Yes, the opposite of relaxing is stressful or busy.

293
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,360
A busy day at work is not relaxing.

294
00:19:18,360 --> 00:19:20,360
A vacation should be relaxing.

295
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:23,200
I agree, 100%.

296
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:24,880
Should we do one more word?

297
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,520
How about booking?

298
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:30,160
Booking, yes, I said I book the hotel early.

299
00:19:30,160 --> 00:19:33,200
To book something means to reserve it,

300
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:36,860
to say, I want this for me on this date.

301
00:19:36,860 --> 00:19:38,560
Can you use it in another sentence?

302
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:41,880
Sure, I need to book a flight to London,

303
00:19:41,880 --> 00:19:45,800
or I booked a table for two at the restaurant.

304
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:49,000
It means you arrange it before you go.

305
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,240
And we often use it with the noun reservation.

306
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:55,200
For example, I have a hotel reservation

307
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:57,900
means the same as I have a booked hotel.

308
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,200
It's very important to book popular.

309
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:11,040
Okay. I think we reviewed many useful words. Souvenir, hiking, spontaneous, dream vacation,

310
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:15,760
local and relaxing. And booking. Don't forget booking.

311
00:20:15,760 --> 00:20:22,020
And booking. Thank you, Jack. I hope that was helpful for everyone. Remember, you can write

312
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:27,120
these words in your notebook. Yes, practice using them. Maybe you can write

313
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:32,360
a sentence about your dream vacation in the comments, using these new words.

314
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:34,800
That is a fantastic idea, Jack.

315
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,480
You are a good teacher.

316
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:37,480
Thank you, Emma.

317
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:38,480
So are you.

318
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,560
Now, let's tell everyone about the question of the day.

319
00:20:41,560 --> 00:20:45,960
Well, Emma, that was a really long and fun conversation.

320
00:20:45,960 --> 00:20:49,400
I almost felt like I was on vacation while we were talking.

321
00:20:49,400 --> 00:20:50,840
Me too, Jack.

322
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:54,240
It was so nice to remember all those good trips.

323
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:58,560
But now it's time to think about our viewers and what we learned today.

324
00:20:58,560 --> 00:20:59,920
Yes, you're right.

325
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:01,160
Let's wrap up.

326
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:06,120
So today's big topic was talking about vacation.

327
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:07,120
That's right.

328
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:13,640
We practiced how to talk about past vacations, like your trip to Greece and my visit to Canada.

329
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:19,440
And we also practiced talking about future vacation dreams, like my dream to go to Brazil

330
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:21,960
and your dream to visit Japan.

331
00:21:21,960 --> 00:21:24,200
We used a lot of useful grammar.

332
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:30,040
We use the past tense a lot, like I visited, I swam, I ate.

333
00:21:30,040 --> 00:21:35,840
And we use the future tense, like I am planning to go, and I want to see.

334
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:37,040
Exactly.

335
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:39,800
And we learned many, many new words.

336
00:21:39,800 --> 00:21:41,520
Let's remember some of them quickly.

337
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:42,520
Okay.

338
00:21:42,520 --> 00:21:47,000
We had souvenir, that's a thing you buy to remember a trip.

339
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:48,940
Like your magnets, Jack.

340
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:52,520
Then we had hiking, that's walking in nature for fun.

341
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:55,320
A word for me is spontaneous.

342
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:58,180
It means doing something without a plan.

343
00:21:58,180 --> 00:22:01,680
And we are not very spontaneous, are we?

344
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:05,020
No, we are planners.

345
00:22:05,020 --> 00:22:07,900
We also talked about dream vacation,

346
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:11,240
which is the best vacation you can imagine.

347
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:15,160
And local, which means from that place,

348
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:18,120
like local food or local people.

349
00:22:18,120 --> 00:22:20,360
And finally, relaxing.

350
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:23,960
That is the most important feeling for a good vacation.

351
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,740
It is.

352
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:28,200
Now, the most important part.

353
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:30,660
We want to hear from you, our viewers.

354
00:22:30,660 --> 00:22:33,780
Yes, it's time for our question of the day.

355
00:22:33,780 --> 00:22:37,260
This is your chance to practice your English writing.

356
00:22:37,260 --> 00:22:40,140
Today's question is all about your dreams.

357
00:22:40,140 --> 00:22:41,140
Are you ready?

358
00:22:41,140 --> 00:22:45,500
The question is, what is your dream vacation?

359
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:48,300
Where do you want to go and why?

360
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:51,940
So tell us about the place you dream of visiting.

361
00:22:51,940 --> 00:22:54,780
What is the name of the country or city?

362
00:22:54,780 --> 00:22:57,300
And tell us why you want to go there.

363
00:22:57,300 --> 00:23:02,180
Is it for the food, the beaches, the history, the cities?

364
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:04,020
For example, you could write,

365
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:06,420
my dream vacation is Egypt.

366
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:09,700
I want to see the pyramids because I love history.

367
00:23:09,700 --> 00:23:13,100
Or my dream vacation is Hawaii.

368
00:23:13,100 --> 00:23:15,620
I want to go there because I love the beach

369
00:23:15,620 --> 00:23:17,140
and warm weather.

370
00:23:17,140 --> 00:23:20,100
Try to use one of our new words if you can.

371
00:23:20,100 --> 00:23:21,380
Maybe you can write,

372
00:23:21,380 --> 00:23:23,940
I want to try the local food in Italy,

373
00:23:23,940 --> 00:23:27,980
or I think hiking in Peru would be amazing.

374
00:23:27,980 --> 00:23:29,940
Don't worry about making mistakes.

375
00:23:29,940 --> 00:23:30,980
It's okay.

376
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:33,300
The most important thing is to try.

377
00:23:33,300 --> 00:23:35,800
We're here to learn together.

378
00:23:35,800 --> 00:23:39,380
We promise to read as many of your comments as we can.

379
00:23:39,380 --> 00:23:42,900
We love reading them and sometimes we even reply.

380
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:44,780
It's so interesting for us to see

381
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:50,460
all the different places you want to visit. The whole world is in the comments.

382
00:23:50,460 --> 00:23:56,240
Before we finish, we have a small request. If you enjoyed this English lesson today,

383
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:57,240
please let us know.

384
00:23:57,240 --> 00:24:01,420
Yes, if the conversation was helpful for you, please click the like button. It's right

385
00:24:01,420 --> 00:24:03,100
below the video.

